F; gate green only if tuned ≥ base on the rubric.\n\n## Acceptance (BDD)\n```gherkin\nFeature: the tuned model is measurably better than its base, honestly\n  Scenario: the eval instrument exists and scores the base first\n    Given the held-out eval set from T2 and a defined rubric\n    When the eval harness runs against the untuned base\n    Then a baseline score is recorded per task category\n\n  Scenario: QLoRA training completes on the proven trainer\n    Given the T2 train split and the T0-proven ROCm device\n    When the QLoRA run executes\n    Then loss is logged, the run completes, and a LoRA adapter is saved\n\n  Scenario: the tuned model beats base on the held-out set\n    Given base and tuned scored by the same rubric with RAG disabled\n    When the eval report is generated\n    Then the tuned model's aggregate score is >= base and the delta is recorded (no unmeasured claims)\n\n  Scenario: the adapter merges to a loadable GGUF\n    Given the trained adapter\n    When it is merged and exported to GGUF\n    Then the GGUF loads in the target runtime without error\n```\n\n## Out of scope\nServing / router wiring (T4), DPO (T5). If tuned does NOT beat base, that is an honest result — log\nit, do not tune the rubric to pass.\n\n## Handoff\nVerifier re-runs `scripts/gates/t3.py`. `docs/train/T3-eval-report.md` is the KR1.5 evidence: base vs\ntuned table per category, the delta, base-model choice, hyperparameters, and dataset provenance.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1695,"cache_read_input_tokens":140194,"output_tokens":1362,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1362,"cache_read_input_tokens":140194,"cache_creation_input_toke